/-!
# Splitting the dimension of a quotient of an adic completion along a prime

Let `B` be a Noetherian ring which is universally catenary, let `J ⊆ B` be an ideal and write
`A' = AdicCompletion J B`. Let `P ⊆ Q` be primes of `B` and let `P' ⊆ Q'` be primes of `A'` lying
over them, with `Q' ∈ V(J A')`. Then the dimension of `(B ⧸ P)_Q` splits as the height of the
image of `P'` in `A' ⧸ P·A'` plus the dimension of `(A' ⧸ P')_{Q'}`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension.height_add_height_quotient_eq_height_quotient_adicCompletion`:
  the dimension splitting at an arbitrary pair `P' ⊆ Q'` with `Q' ∈ V(J A')` over an arbitrary
  Noetherian universally catenary ring, which is the dimension content of the second display of
  [Stacks, Tag 0EHW].
* `Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension.height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient`:
  `height 𝔭 + dim (A' ⧸ P') = dim (B ⧸ P)`, the same splitting when `B` is local, `J ≤ 𝔪_B` and
  `Q'` is the maximal ideal of `A'`.
* `Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension.height_add_height_quotient_eq_height`: the abstract form at an
  outer prime, for a flat extension `A → R` of Noetherian rings with `A` a universally catenary
  domain, `Q' = Q·R` and `R = A + Q'`.
* `Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension.height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_base`: the
  abstract form, for a flat local homomorphism `D → T` of Noetherian local rings with `D` a
  universally catenary domain whose closed fibre is the residue field.

## Implementation notes

The whole content is the abstract form. For a flat local map `D → T` of Noetherian local rings
inducing an isomorphism on residue fields, `dim T = dim D` by the dimension formula
(`Stacks.FlatLocalDimension.ringKrullDim_eq_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`), and the completions
of `D` and of `T` at their maximal ideals are isomorphic by [Stacks, Tag 0AGX]
(`exists_adicCompletion_ringEquiv_of_flat`). When `D` is a universally catenary domain, Ratliff's
theorem (`isUniversallyCatenary_iff_isFormallyCatenary`, Tag 0AW6) makes the spectrum of the
completion of `D` equidimensional, since `⊥` is the only minimal prime; transporting this across
the isomorphism makes the spectrum of the completion of `T` equidimensional. That completion is a
complete Noetherian local ring, hence catenary (Tag 032C), so descent along the flat local map
`T → T^∧` (Tag 0AW4, through `FlatLocalCatenary.height_add_coheight_base`) gives
`height 𝔭 + coheight 𝔭 = dim T` for every prime `𝔭` of `T`.

Equidimensionality is carried in the ring-theoretic spelling `SpecEquidimensional` of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Equidimensional.FlatLocal`; transporting it across a ring isomorphism is
done through `PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv`, under which both `Order.height` and `Order.coheight` are
invariant, so no topological transport lemma is needed.

Locality of `AdicCompletion J B` for `J ≤ 𝔪_B` is not in Mathlib (which treats only `J = 𝔪_B`).
It is proved here as `isLocalRing_adicCompletion_of_le_maximalIdeal`, from the fact that `J·A'` is
the kernel of the surjection `A' → B ⧸ J` and lies in the Jacobson radical.

Nothing is local in the general statement: the two local rings whose dimensions are compared are
`(B ⧸ P)_Q` and `(A' ⧸ P')_{Q'}`, and the abstract form is applied to `D = (B ⧸ P)_Q` and
`T = (A' ⧸ P·A')_{Q'}`. The two hypotheses of the abstract form come from the single fact that
`Q'` is generated by `Q`, which holds because `A' ⧸ J A' = B ⧸ J` and `J ⊆ Q`: that makes
`𝔪_D · T = 𝔪_T`, and since every element of `A'` is congruent to one of `B` modulo `J A' ⊆ Q A'`
it also makes `B ⧸ Q → A' ⧸ Q'` an isomorphism, hence the residue field extension trivial. The
dimensions are read off as heights in the two quotients, which is legitimate because a quotient
of a localization at a prime is a localization of the quotient
(`ringKrullDim_quotient_localizationAtPrime`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AW4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AW4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AW6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AW6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 032C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/032C)
-/

universe u

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

namespace Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension

/-! ### Transporting equidimensionality across a ring isomorphism -/

/-- Equidimensionality of the spectrum transports across a ring isomorphism: the induced order
isomorphism of prime spectra preserves `Order.height` (hence minimality) and `Order.coheight`
(hence the dimension of the quotient by a minimal prime). -/
private theorem specEquidimensional_of_ringEquiv {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (e : R ≃+* S) (h : SpecEquidimensional R) : SpecEquidimensional S := by
  have hht : ∀ x : PrimeSpectrum S,
      Order.height x = Order.height ((PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e).symm x) := fun x => by
    conv_lhs => rw [← OrderIso.apply_symm_apply (PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e) x]
    exact Order.height_orderIso _ _
  have hco : ∀ x : PrimeSpectrum S,
      Order.coheight x = Order.coheight ((PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e).symm x) := fun x => by
    conv_lhs => rw [← OrderIso.apply_symm_apply (PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e) x]
    exact Order.coheight_orderIso _ _
  have hmin : ∀ x : PrimeSpectrum S, x.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes S →
      ((PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e).symm x).asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes R := by
    intro x hx
    have := x.2
    have := ((PrimeSpectrum.comapEquiv e).symm x).2
    refine Ideal.height_eq_zero_iff.mp ?_
    rw [PrimeSpectrum.height_eq_orderHeight, ← hht x, ← PrimeSpectrum.height_eq_orderHeight]
    exact Ideal.height_eq_zero_iff.mpr hx
  intro p hp q hq
  have hpp : p.IsPrime := hp.1.1
  have hqp : q.IsPrime := hq.1.1
  have hgoal := h _ (hmin ⟨p, hpp⟩ hp) _ (hmin ⟨q, hqp⟩ hq)
  rw [← coheight_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient, ← coheight_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient,
    ← hco, ← hco] at hgoal
  exact (coheight_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient ⟨p, hpp⟩).symm.trans
    (hgoal.trans (coheight_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient ⟨q, hqp⟩))

/-! ### Equidimensionality of the completion of a universally catenary local domain -/

/-- For a Noetherian local domain which is universally catenary, the spectrum of its completion
at the maximal ideal is equidimensional. This is Ratliff's theorem at the only minimal prime of a
domain, namely `⊥`. -/
@[ega "IV 7.8.3" "more general"]
private theorem specEquidimensional_adicCompletion_of_isUniversallyCatenary (D : Type u)
    [CommRing D] [IsNoetherianRing D] [IsLocalRing D] [IsDomain D]
    (hcat : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary D) :
    SpecEquidimensional (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal D) D) := by
  have hbot : (⊥ : Ideal D) ∈ minimalPrimes D := by
    rw [IsDomain.minimalPrimes_eq_singleton_bot]
    exact Set.mem_singleton _
  have h := (isUniversallyCatenary_iff_isFormallyCatenary D).mp hcat ⊥ hbot
  rw [Ideal.map_bot] at h
  exact specEquidimensional_of_ringEquiv (RingEquiv.quotientBot _)
    (specEquidimensional_iff_equidimensional.mpr h)

/-! ### The height-plus-coheight identity from equidimensionality of the completion -/

/-- If the spectrum of the completion of a Noetherian local ring `T` at its maximal ideal is
equidimensional, then `height 𝔭 + coheight 𝔭 = dim T` for every prime `𝔭` of `T`. The completion
is a complete Noetherian local ring, hence catenary, and `T → T^∧` is flat and local, so this is
[Stacks, Tag 0AW4]. -/
private theorem height_add_coheight_eq_height_top (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [IsNoetherianRing T]
    [IsLocalRing T] (hequi : SpecEquidimensional (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal T) T))
    (𝔭 : PrimeSpectrum T) :
    Order.height 𝔭 + Order.coheight 𝔭 = Order.height (⊤ : PrimeSpectrum T) := by
  have hUC : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal T) T) :=
    isUniversallyCatenary_of_isPrecomplete_maximalIdeal _
  have hcat := Ring.isCatenary_iff_isCatenarySpace_primeSpectrum.mp
    (hUC (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal T) T))
  exact FlatLocalCatenary.height_add_coheight_base
    (maximalIdeal_comap (algebraMap T (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal T) T)))
    (FlatLocalCatenary.coheight_covBy_of_isCatenarySpace hcat) hequi 𝔭

/-! ### The abstract dimension splitting -/

/-- **The dimension of a universally catenary Noetherian local domain splits along a prime of a
flat local extension with trivial closed fibre.** If `D → T` is a flat local homomorphism of
Noetherian local rings with `D` a universally catenary domain, `𝔪_D·T = 𝔪_T` and the induced map
of residue fields an isomorphism, then for every prime `𝔭` of `T`,
`height 𝔭 + dim (T ⧸ 𝔭) = dim D`. -/
@[ega "IV 5.5.1" "special case"]
theorem height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_base {D T : Type u} [CommRing D]
    [CommRing T] [IsNoetherianRing D] [IsNoetherianRing T] [IsLocalRing D] [IsLocalRing T]
    [IsDomain D] [Algebra D T] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap D T)] [Module.Flat D T]
    (hcat : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary D)
    (hmax : (maximalIdeal D).map (algebraMap D T) = maximalIdeal T)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (ResidueField.map (algebraMap D T)))
    (𝔭 : Ideal T) [𝔭.IsPrime] :
    (𝔭.height : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (T ⧸ 𝔭) = ringKrullDim D := by
  have hequi : SpecEquidimensional (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal T) T) := by
    obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := exists_adicCompletion_ringEquiv_of_flat
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal D)) hmax hres
    exact specEquidimensional_of_ringEquiv e
      (specEquidimensional_adicCompletion_of_isUniversallyCatenary D hcat)
  have hkey := height_add_coheight_eq_height_top T hequi (⟨𝔭, ‹𝔭.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum T)
  have hdim : ringKrullDim D = ringKrullDim T :=
    Stacks.FlatLocalDimension.ringKrullDim_eq_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq hmax
  have hh : 𝔭.height = Order.height (⟨𝔭, ‹𝔭.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum T) :=
    PrimeSpectrum.height_eq_orderHeight (⟨𝔭, ‹𝔭.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum T)
  have hc := coheight_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient (⟨𝔭, ‹𝔭.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum T)
  have ht : (Order.height (⊤ : PrimeSpectrum T) : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim T := by
    rw [← PrimeSpectrum.height_eq_orderHeight (⊤ : PrimeSpectrum T)]
    exact IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim
  rw [hh, ← hc, hdim, ← ht, ← WithBot.coe_add, hkey]

/-! ### Locality of an adic completion at an ideal inside the maximal ideal -/

/-- The `J`-adic completion of a Noetherian local ring is local when `J` lies in the maximal
ideal: the ideal `J·A'` is the kernel of the surjection onto `B ⧸ J` and lies in the Jacobson
radical, so every maximal ideal of `A'` is the preimage of a maximal ideal of the local ring
`B ⧸ J`. -/
theorem isLocalRing_adicCompletion_of_le_maximalIdeal {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] (J : Ideal R) (hJ : J ≤ maximalIdeal R) :
    IsLocalRing (AdicCompletion J R) := by
  classical
  have hJfg : J.FG := Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing J
  let Sc := AdicCompletion J R
  let f : Sc →+* R ⧸ J := (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J).toRingHom
  have hfsurj : Function.Surjective f := AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ_surjective J
  have hker : RingHom.ker f = J.map (algebraMap R Sc) :=
    AdicCompletion.ker_evalOneₐ_eq_map J hJfg
  have hJne : J ≠ ⊤ := fun h => (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (h ▸ hJ))
  have _ : Nontrivial (R ⧸ J) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hJne
  have _ : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ J) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hcomplete : IsAdicComplete (J.map (algebraMap R Sc)) Sc :=
    AdicCompletion.isAdicComplete_self J hJfg
  have hjac : J.map (algebraMap R Sc) ≤ Ideal.jacobson (⊥ : Ideal Sc) :=
    IsAdicComplete.le_jacobson_bot _
  have hmax : ((maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R Sc)).IsMaximal :=
    AdicCompletion.isMaximal_map_of_le J (maximalIdeal R) hJ hJfg
  have hkerM : RingHom.ker f ≤ (maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R Sc) :=
    hker ▸ Ideal.map_mono hJ
  have hrecover : ∀ L : Ideal Sc, RingHom.ker f ≤ L → (L.map f).comap f = L := by
    intro L hL
    rw [Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective f hfsurj,
      sup_eq_left.mpr (by simpa only [RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot] using hL)]
  refine IsLocalRing.of_unique_max_ideal
    ⟨(maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R Sc), hmax, ?_⟩
  intro K hK
  have hkerK : RingHom.ker f ≤ K := by
    rw [hker]
    refine hjac.trans ?_
    change sInf {L : Ideal Sc | (⊥ : Ideal Sc) ≤ L ∧ L.IsMaximal} ≤ K
    exact sInf_le ⟨bot_le, hK⟩
  calc K = (K.map f).comap f := (hrecover K hkerK).symm
    _ = (maximalIdeal (R ⧸ J)).comap f := by
        rw [IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.IsMaximal.map_of_surjective_of_ker_le hfsurj hkerK)]
    _ = (((maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R Sc)).map f).comap f := by
        rw [IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.IsMaximal.map_of_surjective_of_ker_le hfsurj hkerM)]
    _ = (maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R Sc) := hrecover _ hkerM

/-- The maximal ideal of the `J`-adic completion of a Noetherian local ring, for `J` inside the
maximal ideal, is generated by the image of the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem maximalIdeal_adicCompletion {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] (J : Ideal R) (hJ : J ≤ maximalIdeal R) :
    have := isLocalRing_adicCompletion_of_le_maximalIdeal J hJ
    maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion J R) =
      (maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion J R)) :=
  have := isLocalRing_adicCompletion_of_le_maximalIdeal J hJ
  (IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal
    (AdicCompletion.isMaximal_map_of_le J (maximalIdeal R) hJ
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing J))).symm

/-- Every element of the `J`-adic completion agrees with an element of the base modulo `J·A'`:
`J·A'` is the kernel of the surjection onto `R ⧸ J`. -/
private theorem exists_sub_mem_map_adicCompletion {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (J : Ideal R) (x : AdicCompletion J R) :
    ∃ a : R, x - algebraMap R (AdicCompletion J R) a ∈
      J.map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion J R)) := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := J) (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J x)
  refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
  rw [← AdicCompletion.ker_evalOneₐ_eq_map J (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing J)]
  have hcomp : (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J) (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion J R) a) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk J a :=
    RingHom.congr_fun (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ_comp_algebraMap_eq_mk J) a
  change (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J).toRingHom _ = 0
  rw [RingHom.map_sub]
  change (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J) x - (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J) _ = 0
  rw [hcomp, ← ha, sub_self]

/-! ### The dimension splitting for a quotient of an adic completion -/

/-- **The second display of [Stacks, Tag 0EHW].** Let `B` be a universally catenary Noetherian
local ring, let `J ≤ 𝔪_B`, write `A' = AdicCompletion J B` and let `P'` be a prime of `A'` lying
over a prime `P` of `B`. Then the height of the image of `P'` in `A' ⧸ P·A'` plus the dimension
of `A' ⧸ P'` is the dimension of `B ⧸ P`. -/
theorem height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_quotient
    {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B] [IsLocalRing B]
    (hcat : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary B)
    {J : Ideal B} (hJ : J ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
    (P : Ideal B) [P.IsPrime]
    (P' : Ideal (AdicCompletion J B)) [P'.IsPrime] [P'.LiesOver P] :
    ((P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).height :
        WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P') = ringKrullDim (B ⧸ P) := by
  have hlocA' := isLocalRing_adicCompletion_of_le_maximalIdeal J hJ
  have hmA' := maximalIdeal_adicCompletion J hJ
  -- `P·A' ≤ P'`, because `P'` lies over `P`
  have hPP' : P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤ P' :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr (Ideal.LiesOver.over (p := P) (P := P')).le
  -- `P·A'` and `𝔪_B·A'` sit inside the maximal ideal of `A'`
  have hIle : P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤
      maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion J B) := by
    rw [hmA']
    exact Ideal.map_mono (le_maximalIdeal ‹P.IsPrime›.ne_top)
  -- instances on the two quotients
  have : Nontrivial (B ⧸ P) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr ‹P.IsPrime›.ne_top
  have : IsLocalRing (B ⧸ P) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk P) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : Nontrivial (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) :=
    FlatLocalCatenary.quot_nontrivial_of_le hIle
  have : IsLocalRing (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : Module.Flat (B ⧸ P)
      (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) :=
    FlatLocalCatenary.flat_quot P
  -- the closed fibre of `B ⧸ P → A' ⧸ P·A'` is the residue field
  have hmax : (maximalIdeal (B ⧸ P)).map (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
      (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))) =
      maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) := by
    rw [← FlatLocalCatenary.map_maximalIdeal_quot P, Ideal.map_map,
      FlatLocalCatenary.algebraMap_quot_comp, ← Ideal.map_map, ← hmA',
      FlatLocalCatenary.map_maximalIdeal_quot]
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
      (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))) :=
    ((IsLocalRing.local_hom_TFAE _).out 1 3).mpr (le_of_eq hmax)
  have : IsDomain (B ⧸ P) := Ideal.Quotient.isDomain P
  -- the residue fields agree
  have hres : Function.Bijective (ResidueField.map (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
      (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))) := by
    refine ⟨RingHom.injective _, fun y => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := residue_surjective y
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (I := P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) t
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := exists_sub_mem_map_adicCompletion J a
    refine ⟨residue (B ⧸ P) (Ideal.Quotient.mk P b), ?_⟩
    rw [ResidueField.map_residue, ← ht]
    apply (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem _ _).mpr
    have hmem : algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B) b - a ∈
        (maximalIdeal B).map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) := by
      have h0 := (Ideal.map_mono (f := algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) hJ) hb
      simpa only [neg_sub] using neg_mem h0
    rw [← ha, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient, ← map_sub,
      ← FlatLocalCatenary.map_maximalIdeal_quot (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))),
      hmA']
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hmem
  -- the abstract splitting, and the identification `(A' ⧸ P·A') ⧸ 𝔭 ≅ A' ⧸ P'`
  have : (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).IsPrime :=
    Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime hPP'
  have hsplit := height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_base
    (D := B ⧸ P) (T := AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))
    (Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary.of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective hcat) hmax hres
    (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))))
  rwa [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE hPP')] at hsplit

/-! ### A quotient of a localization at a prime is a localization of the quotient -/

/-- **The dimension of `(R ⧸ 𝔭)_𝔮`, read on `R_𝔮 ⧸ 𝔭 R_𝔮`.** For an ideal `𝔭` inside a prime `𝔮`
of `R`, the ring `R_𝔮 ⧸ 𝔭 R_𝔮` is a localization of `R ⧸ 𝔭` at the image of `𝔮`, so its Krull
dimension is the height of that image. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_localizationAtPrime {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    (p q : Ideal R) [q.IsPrime] (hpq : p ≤ q) :
    ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ p.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q))) =
      ((q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p)).height : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hcomap := Ideal.comap_map_mk hpq
  have _ : (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p)).IsPrime := Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime hpq
  have _ : (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p)).LiesOver q := ⟨hcomap.symm⟩
  have hsub : Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (R ⧸ p) q.primeCompl =
      (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p)).primeCompl :=
    Ideal.algebraMapSubmonoid_primeCompl_of_liesOver_surjective _ q Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have _ : IsLocalization (q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p)).primeCompl
      (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ p.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q))) :=
    hsub ▸ inferInstance
  exact IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height _ _

/-! ### Trivial residue field extension from an isomorphism of the quotients -/

/-- **A map inducing an isomorphism of the quotients induces an isomorphism of the residue
fields.** If `𝔮 = f⁻¹(𝔮')` and every element of `S` is congruent modulo `𝔮'` to one in the image
of `f`, then the extension `κ(𝔮) → κ(𝔮')` is bijective: it is injective because it is a map of
fields, and surjective because a fraction `x/s` of `S_{𝔮'}` has the same residue as the image of
a fraction `a/b` of `R_𝔮` chosen with `x ≡ f a` and `s ≡ f b` modulo `𝔮'`. -/
private theorem bijective_residueFieldMap {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) (q : Ideal R) [q.IsPrime] (q' : Ideal S) [q'.IsPrime]
    (hq : q = q'.comap f) (hsurj : ∀ x : S, ∃ r : R, x - f r ∈ q')
    (g : Localization.AtPrime q →+* Localization.AtPrime q') [IsLocalHom g]
    (hg : ∀ r : R, g (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) r) =
      algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime q') (f r)) :
    Function.Bijective (ResidueField.map g) := by
  have hfq : ∀ b : q.primeCompl, (f b : S) ∈ q'.primeCompl := fun b hb => b.2 (hq ▸ hb)
  have hgmk : ∀ (a : R) (b : q.primeCompl),
      g (IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q) a b) =
        IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q') (f a) ⟨f b, hfq b⟩ := by
    intro a b
    rw [IsLocalization.eq_mk'_iff_mul_eq]
    change g (IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q) a b) *
      algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime q') (f (b : R)) = _
    rw [← hg (b : R), ← map_mul, IsLocalization.mk'_spec]
    exact hg a
  refine ⟨RingHom.injective _, ?_⟩
  intro y
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := residue_surjective (R := Localization.AtPrime q') y
  obtain ⟨⟨x, s⟩, hxs⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective q'.primeCompl t
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hsurj x
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hsurj (s : S)
  have hbq : b ∈ q.primeCompl := by
    intro hbq
    rw [hq] at hbq
    exact s.2 (by simpa using add_mem hb (Ideal.mem_comap.mp hbq))
  refine ⟨residue _ (IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q) a ⟨b, hbq⟩), ?_⟩
  rw [ResidueField.map_residue, hgmk, ← ht, ← hxs]
  refine (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem _ _).mpr ?_
  rw [← IsLocalization.mk'_sub]
  refine (IsLocalization.AtPrime.mk'_mem_maximal_iff _ q' _ _).mpr ?_
  rw [show f a * (s : S) - x * f b = f a * ((s : S) - f b) - (x - f a) * f b by ring]
  exact sub_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hb) (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ha)

/-! ### The abstract dimension splitting at an outer prime -/

/-- **The dimension of a universally catenary Noetherian domain splits along a prime of a flat
extension generated at an outer prime.** Let `A` be a Noetherian universally catenary domain, let
`R` be a Noetherian flat `A`-algebra, and let `Q'` be a prime of `R` over a prime `Q` of `A` with
`Q' = Q·R` and `R = A + Q'`. Then for every prime `P' ⊆ Q'` of `R`,
`height P' + dim ((R ⧸ P')_{Q'}) = height Q`.

The two hypotheses on `Q'` say exactly that the flat local homomorphism `A_Q → R_{Q'}` has the
residue field of `A_Q` as its closed fibre, so this is
`height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_base` read at `D = A_Q` and `T = R_{Q'}`. -/
theorem height_add_height_quotient_eq_height
    {A R : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsDomain A] [Algebra A R] [Module.Flat A R]
    (hcat : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary A)
    (Q : Ideal A) [Q.IsPrime] (Q' : Ideal R) [Q'.IsPrime] [Q'.LiesOver Q]
    (hQ' : Q.map (algebraMap A R) = Q')
    (hsurj : ∀ x : R, ∃ a : A, x - algebraMap A R a ∈ Q')
    (P' : Ideal R) [P'.IsPrime] (hP' : P' ≤ Q') :
    P'.height + (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P')).height = Q.height := by
  let : Algebra (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q') :=
    Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver Q Q'
  have hflat : Module.Flat (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q') :=
    (Module.flat_iff_of_isLocalization (R := A) (Localization.AtPrime Q) Q.primeCompl
      (Localization.AtPrime Q')).mpr inferInstance
  have hcatD : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary (Localization.AtPrime Q) :=
    Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary.localization Q.primeCompl _ hcat
  have hmax : (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime Q)).map
      (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q')) =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime Q') := by
    have h2 : (Q.map (algebraMap A R)).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime Q')) =
        Q'.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime Q')) := by rw [hQ']
    rw [Ideal.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A R (Localization.AtPrime Q')] at h2
    rw [← IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal Q (Localization.AtPrime Q),
      ← IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal Q' (Localization.AtPrime Q'),
      Ideal.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A (Localization.AtPrime Q)
        (Localization.AtPrime Q'), h2]
  have hres : Function.Bijective (ResidueField.map
      (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q'))) :=
    bijective_residueFieldMap (algebraMap A R) Q Q' Ideal.LiesOver.over hsurj _
      (fun a => by
        rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q'),
          IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A R (Localization.AtPrime Q')])
  have hdisj : Disjoint (Q'.primeCompl : Set R) (P' : Set R) :=
    Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ ha hb => ha (hP' hb)
  have : (P'.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime Q'))).IsPrime :=
    IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint Q'.primeCompl _ P' inferInstance hdisj
  have key := height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_base
    (D := Localization.AtPrime Q) (T := Localization.AtPrime Q') hcatD hmax hres
    (P'.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime Q')))
  rw [IsLocalization.height_map_of_disjoint Q'.primeCompl P' hdisj,
    ringKrullDim_quotient_localizationAtPrime P' Q' hP',
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height Q (Localization.AtPrime Q)] at key
  exact_mod_cast key

/-! ### The dimension splitting for an adic completion at an arbitrary outer prime -/

/-- **The dimension content of the second display of [Stacks, Tag 0EHW].** Let `B` be a Noetherian
universally catenary ring, let `J ⊆ B` be an ideal and write `A' = AdicCompletion J B`. Let
`P' ⊆ Q'` be primes of `A'` with `J A' ⊆ Q'`, lying over primes `P ⊆ Q` of `B`. Then the height
of the image of `P'` in `A' ⧸ P·A'` plus the dimension of `(A' ⧸ P')_{Q'}` is the dimension of
`(B ⧸ P)_Q`, all three read as heights.

Because `A' ⧸ J A' = B ⧸ J` and `J ⊆ Q`, the prime `Q'` is generated by `Q` and every element of
`A'` is congruent to one of `B` modulo `Q A'`; passing to the quotients by `P` and `P·A'` this is
`height_add_height_quotient_eq_height` for the flat extension `B ⧸ P → A' ⧸ P·A'`. -/
theorem height_add_height_quotient_eq_height_quotient_adicCompletion
    {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    (hcat : Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary B) {J : Ideal B}
    (P Q : Ideal B) [P.IsPrime] [Q.IsPrime]
    (P' : Ideal (AdicCompletion J B)) [P'.IsPrime] [P'.LiesOver P]
    (Q' : Ideal (AdicCompletion J B)) [Q'.IsPrime] [Q'.LiesOver Q]
    (hJQ' : J.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤ Q') (hPQ' : P' ≤ Q') :
    (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).height +
        (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P')).height = (Q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P)).height := by
  have hPover : P = P'.comap (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) := Ideal.LiesOver.over
  have hQover : Q = Q'.comap (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) := Ideal.LiesOver.over
  have hPQ : P ≤ Q := hPover.le.trans ((Ideal.comap_mono hPQ').trans_eq hQover.symm)
  have hI₀P' : P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤ P' :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hPover.le
  have hI₀Q' : P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤ Q' := hI₀P'.trans hPQ'
  have hQQ' : Q.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) ≤ Q' :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hQover.le
  have hJQ : J ≤ Q := (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hJQ').trans_eq hQover.symm
  -- every element of `A'` is congruent to one of `B` modulo `Q A'`
  have hBQ' : ∀ x : AdicCompletion J B, ∃ b : B,
      x - algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B) b ∈ Q.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_sub_mem_map_adicCompletion J x
    exact ⟨a, Ideal.map_mono hJQ ha⟩
  -- hence `Q'` is generated by `Q`
  have hQmap : Q.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) = Q' := by
    refine le_antisymm hQQ' ?_
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hBQ' x
    have h1 : algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B) b ∈ Q' := by
      have h := sub_mem hx (hQQ' hb)
      simpa using h
    have h2 : b ∈ Q := by rw [hQover]; exact h1
    have h3 := add_mem (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)) h2) hb
    simpa using h3
  have : Module.Flat B (AdicCompletion J B) := AdicCompletion.flat_of_isNoetherian J
  have : Module.Flat (B ⧸ P)
      (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) :=
    FlatLocalCatenary.flat_quot P
  have : IsDomain (B ⧸ P) := Ideal.Quotient.isDomain P
  have : (Q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P)).IsPrime :=
    Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime hPQ
  have : (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).IsPrime :=
    Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime hI₀Q'
  have : (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).IsPrime :=
    Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime hI₀P'
  have halg := FlatLocalCatenary.algebraMap_quot_comp (A := B) (B := AdicCompletion J B) P
  have hq0map : (Q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P)).map
      (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
        (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))) =
      Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map, halg, ← Ideal.map_map, hQmap]
  have hc2 := Ideal.comap_map_mk hI₀Q'
  have hc3 : (((Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).comap
      (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
        (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))))).comap
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk P) = Q := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap, halg, ← Ideal.comap_comap, hc2, ← hQover]
  have : (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).LiesOver
      (Q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P)) := by
    refine ⟨?_⟩
    have h := Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk P) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      ((Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).comap
        (algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
          (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))))
    rw [hc3] at h
    rw [Ideal.under_def]
    exact h
  have hsurjR : ∀ x : AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)),
      ∃ a : B ⧸ P, x - algebraMap (B ⧸ P) _ a ∈
        Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))) := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (I := P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))) x
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hBQ' y
    refine ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk P b, ?_⟩
    have hcomm : algebraMap (B ⧸ P)
        (AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk P b) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))
          (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B) b) := RingHom.congr_fun halg b
    rw [hcomm, ← map_sub]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (hQmap ▸ hb)
  have main := height_add_height_quotient_eq_height
    (A := B ⧸ P) (R := AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))
    (Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary.of_surjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective hcat)
    (Q.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P))
    (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))) hq0map hsurjR
    (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))))
    (Ideal.map_mono hPQ')
  -- the second summand is read on `A' ⧸ P'` instead of on `(A' ⧸ P·A') ⧸ (P' ⧸ P·A')`
  have htrans : ((Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).map
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))))).height =
      (Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P')).height := by
    have himg : ((Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))).map
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk
          (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))))).map
        ((DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE hI₀P' :
          _ ≃+* AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P') : _ →+* AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P') =
        Q'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P') := by
      have hcomp : ((DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE hI₀P' :
            _ ≃+* AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P') : _ →+* AdicCompletion J B ⧸ P').comp
          ((Ideal.Quotient.mk
              (P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B)))))).comp
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.map (algebraMap B (AdicCompletion J B))))) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk P' :=
        DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE_comp_quotQuotMk hI₀P'
      rw [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, RingHom.comp_assoc, hcomp]
    rw [← himg]
    exact (RingEquiv.height_map _ _).symm
  rw [htrans] at main
  exact main

end Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension

